Three things the upstream draft did not have.

SAP_ASSETS_DIR points the signer at a directory the operator fills in, for
deployments whose egress never reaches swcdn.apple.com — a Space behind a
filter, a host in a region where Apple's CDN is unreliable. Without it the
only path to a working sign-in was a download that could not happen.

sap-assets.json alongside the binaries overrides the built-in asset list. It
is what makes the manual path verifiable rather than hopeful, and it is how a
deployment points the signer at a different build of those binaries.

A fetch that cannot connect now says so. Node collapses every failure into
"fetch failed" with the reason on .cause; unwrapped, an operator got two
useless words and no hint that another path existed.

Also covers the routes and the verification with tests — 19 of them, offline,
using stand-in files described by a manifest rather than 38 MB of Apple's
binaries — and fixes SapStatus eating a track of ProductDetail's action grid.
